=== §1. Quadrics defining V ⊂ P^6 ===
  Q1 = -a**2 - b**2 + d**2
  Q2 = -b**2 - c**2 + e**2
  Q3 = -a**2 - c**2 + f**2
  Q4 = -a**2 - b**2 - c**2 + g**2

=== §2. S_3 action on (a,b,c) + induced on (d,e,f) ===
  perm (a,b,c) -> (abc): OK
  perm (a,b,c) -> (acb): OK
  perm (a,b,c) -> (bac): OK
  perm (a,b,c) -> (bca): OK
  perm (a,b,c) -> (cab): OK
  perm (a,b,c) -> (cba): OK
  S_3 preservation: 6/6

=== §3. Sign-flip (Z/2)^7 action ===
  a -> -a preserves all 4 quadrics: OK
  By symmetry (each Q is sum of squares of subset of vars),
  full (Z/2)^7 sign-flip group preserves I_V.
  |sign-flip subgroup| = 2^7 = 128
  In PGL(7): quotient by diagonal => effective sign group is (Z/2)^6 of order 64

=== §4. Total obvious Aut_lin(V) ⊂ PGL(7) ===
  G_obvious = S_3 ⋉ (Z/2)^6 of order 6 * 64 = 384
  (semidirect: S_3 permutes the 7 sign-flip generators consistently)

=== §5. Infinitesimal stabilizer (Lie algebra) ===
  Computing the linear stabilizer of I in gl(7) ...
  # quadratic monomial constraints: 73 (deduplicated)
  Total free parameters before constraints: 65
  Dimension of linear stabilizer (Lie alg): 1
  Free symbols in M: ['m_1_1']

  Substituted M:
⎡m₁ ₁   0     0     0     0     0     0  ⎤
